</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>The Role of ASR for Translation Performance</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To determine whether the ASR objective competes for model capacity or provides beneficial regularization, we conducted a task-ablation study. We trained a version of Hikari-medium using the same dataset and hyperparameters but removed the transcription task entirely, leaving only the English-to-Japanese, German, and Russian translation objectives.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results in Table <a href="#A3.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ C.3 The Role of ASR for Translation Performance ‣ Appendix C Extended Ablation Studies: Model Size and Encoder Variants ‣ Streaming Translation and Transcription Through Speech-to-Text Causal Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> demonstrate that translation-only models perform consistently worse than their multitask counterpart. In the high-quality podcast domain, we observed drops of up to 5.85 BLEU points and a marked increase in latency. The performance gap was even more pronounced in the IWSLT25Instruct set, where BLEU scores plummeted by as much as 15.98 points, accompanied by a doubling of StreamLAAL values in some instances.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We hypothesize that the ASR task serves as an anchor for the causal encoder. By forcing the model to reconstruct the source text, it preserves acoustic features that might otherwise be lost if the model is optimized solely for semantic abstractions. This grounding seems to be important for the <span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">WAIT</span> token mechanism, as accurate READ/WRITE decisions rely on the model’s ability to precisely detect word boundaries and silences in the incoming audio stream.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Effect of excluding the ASR task from training. StreamLAAL CA is shown in brackets. The values represent the BLEU and latency difference between Hikari-medium trained with <em id="A3.T8.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> tasks and Hikari-medium trained without the ASR task.</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T8.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
